Q: javascript execution events order A: <p>You can use setTimeout function.  It has two parameters. The first one is your function, the other's time (ms). When time is up which is defined, function will run.</p>

<p><a href="http://www.w3schools.com/jsref/met_win_settimeout.asp" rel="nofollow">More details here</a></p>

<pre><code>var ms = 2000;
document.getElementById("alertProg").style.display='block';
setTimeout(function(){
    document.getElementById("alertProg").style.display='none';
},ms);
</code></pre>
